From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:03:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llama-cpp): embed the token ids Embedding is given

/v1/embeddings accepts token ids, and core/backend/embeddings.go sends
them to the backend in PredictOptions.EmbeddingTokens, leaving the text
field empty. The llama.cpp backend never reads that field: it embeds the
empty text, which it then refuses ("Input content cannot be empty"). A
client cannot embed tokens at all, and so cannot truncate an input to
exactly N tokens of the model's own tokenizer. Cutting the text instead
is not exact: a prefix of a text does not always tokenize to a prefix of
its tokens, and a detokenized prefix does not always tokenize back to
the same tokens (3 of 512 multilingual texts at 1,024 tokens, bge-m3).

Embed the ids. They are the input's tokens as TokenizeString returns
them, without special tokens, so they get the special tokens a text
gets: a probe text is tokenized with and without them, and the ids take
the place of its own tokens (embedding_tokens.h, with a unit test).
Embedding a text's tokens is then embedding the text, bit for bit; a
request with text only is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
